;;! Sys.Platform - the numbers this target's kernel uses: syscall
;;! numbers, open and socket flags, errno values, poll and signal
;;! constants and struct layouts. One file per target; every file
;;! declares the same names, and the build picks the one for the
;;! target being compiled for (this one is `baremetal-aarch64`).
; Sys.Platform - bare metal on AArch64 (QEMU's `virt` machine).
;
; Selected by the `.baremetal-aarch64.ax` filename suffix when compiling
; for `--target=baremetal-aarch64`.
;
; THIS IS THE THIRD KIND OF PLATFORM MODULE. The POSIX modules are
; tables of integers and `Sys.ax` makes every kernel call itself; the
; Windows module answers `usesSyscallAbi` 0 and does the work itself
; over `extern "kernel32"` bindings. This module answers the same 0
; and does the work itself over the PL011 UART at 0x09000000 - with no
; `extern` block at all, because there is nothing on the device that
; could provide one. `Sys.ax` calls `platformWriteFd`,
; `platformReadFd` and `platformExitWith` where it would otherwise have
; called `__syscallN`; what is NOT routed that way (files, processes,
; sockets, the clock, entropy, signals) reaches its `__syscallN` arm,
; which the compiler lowers here to a trap (`axiom: no syscall ABI on
; this target`, status 74) rather than to an `svc` instruction no
; kernel would answer. Loud, and on purpose - the Windows module's
; phase-1 shape, with the UART where its console half is.
;
; THE DESCRIPTOR CALLS ANSWER `Err` RATHER THAN TRAPPING wherever the
; answer fits in the type. There is no input device, so a read is
; ENOSYS; descriptors other than 1 and 2 name nothing, so a write to
; one is EBADF; there is no clock, so `clockHasMonotonic` is 0 and the
; monotonic query answers ENOSYS without a syscall. What cannot fit -
; an `open`, a `fork`, a `socket` - traps through `__syscallN` like
; its Windows twin.
;
; THE WORD-WIDTH AND EFFECT RULES the Windows module states hold with
; the UART in place of the HANDLEs. Descriptors 1 and 2 are the UART;
; any other value is refused. None of the three shims claims
; `effect(io)`, because the walk cannot see a store to a memory-mapped
; register: `__store8v` is `Mut`, not `IO` (its row matches `__store8`
; in every respect but the emitted `volatile`), and claiming `io` over
; it is AX3010. The POSIX modules are untagged for the same reason - a
; constant performs nothing - so this module tags nothing either.
;
; `Err` for the `(Result Int Error)` the two descriptor calls answer;
; acyclic, as the five syscall-ABI files record.
(import Err)

;; Sys.Platform - Darwin (macOS) syscall numbers and flags.
(pub :: sysReadNum Int)
(pub fn (sysReadNum)
  0)

